he range of $x.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262750 1113 #uuid "3c676d06-dd78-5ee3-bb23-3607dba288b2" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262750 1145 "To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t+1)-2 \\\\  & =2(t-1)^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2(t-1)^{2}\\ge 0,$ we can conclude that\n\n$$\nx\\ge -2.\n$$" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262751 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262752 13194139533873 true] [17592186262751 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533873 true] [17592186262751 1041 "field-1" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262751 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262752 13194139533873 true] [17592186262751 1110 #uuid "81861ba9-0c02-5338-a6b1-ac4cd73882ed" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262752 1034 "\\ge" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533873 true] [17592186262752 1111 #uuid "03d2e027-12bc-5336-8af7-7f10422196b2" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262754 13194139533873 true] [17592186262753 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533873 true] [17592186262753 1041 "field-2" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262753 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262754 13194139533873 true] [17592186262753 1110 #uuid "c01ba207-8fb0-5b93-a879-b917578a8428" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262754 1034 "-2" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533873 true] [17592186262754 1111 #uuid "269d5eef-bd03-59a7-9703-c23e3b4bbea6" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262756 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262758 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262760 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262762 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262764 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262766 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1089 "q-327871" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1100 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le $\n{{field-3}}.\n\n \n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1113 #uuid "c03dd84c-7dcb-5b32-88d9-686df43c4951" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262755 1145 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le x\\le \\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{5}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4} & \\le \\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}+2 & \\le \\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\le \\frac{3}{4}+2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & \\le y\\le \\frac{11}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $\\frac{5}{4}\\le y\\le \\frac{11}{4}.$" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262756 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262757 13194139533873 true] [17592186262756 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533873 true] [17592186262756 1041 "field-1" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262756 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262757 13194139533873 true] [17592186262756 1110 #uuid "53e8e60b-e158-531f-b5ad-3a67ad67c8be" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262757 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533873 true] [17592186262757 11